<title>USA: Vermont's full Senate to meet on property taxes.</title>
<headline>Vermont's full Senate to meet on property taxes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vermont's Senate will hold a rare meeting this week, gathering as a Committee of the Whole, in an unusual step prompted by a state Supreme Court ruling.</p>
<p>The state court ruled that Vermont's way of funding public education with local property taxes was unconstitutional.</p>
<p>So the legislature has to find a new funding scheme that goes beyond the modest efforts at property tax reform that had been contemplated.</p>
<p>All of the state senators are expected to attend the meeting which will include briefings by the lawyers involved in the Supreme Court case.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
